thermonuclear.structure.controller=Front centre, middle layer; offset (1,1,0)
thermonuclear.structure.box=3x3x3: 1 controller, 25 heat-proof casing positions, 1 internal air block. Each hatch replaces one casing, not an extra block.
thermonuclear.structure.hatches=Compatible GT IO hatches, including ME, DEBUG, dual input, multi-amp and wireless dynamos. No maintenance required.
thermonuclear.structure.nuclear.controller=Export position E, facing out of the wall; rotated structure offset (4,21,11), not the scanner offset.
thermonuclear.structure.nuclear.blocks=B: reinforced glass; C: reinforced concrete; D: steel frames; F/H: source water.
thermonuclear.structure.nuclear.pipes=A: 18 matching-tier item pipe casings, 8 tiers from tin to black plutonium. Tier is an independent upgrade attribute.
thermonuclear.structure.nuclear.services=G: 17 concrete or item bus, dynamo, optional maintenance positions; compatible subclasses accepted, fluid and dual input hatches rejected.
thermonuclear.structure.nuclear.coolant_io=The two I positions require exactly one fluid input hatch and one fluid output hatch.
thermonuclear.structure.heat_exchange.box=9×14×7: controller faces outward; D is solid steel machine casing and E is bronze pipe casing.
thermonuclear.structure.heat_exchange.cold_input=A: cold-fluid input hatch; distilled water is read from this position.
thermonuclear.structure.heat_exchange.cold_output=B: cold-fluid output hatch; cooled fluid is sent to this position.
thermonuclear.structure.heat_exchange.hot_input=C: hot-fluid input hatch; hot coolant is read from this position.
thermonuclear.structure.heat_exchange.hot_output=F: hot-fluid output hatch; steam is sent to this position.
